<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Basel (1499)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1499">1499</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Basel (1499) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-war">Swabian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Basel of 22 September 1499 ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-war">Swabian War</a> between the Old Swiss Confederacy and Emperor Maximilian I with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-league">Swabian League</a>. It freed the Confederates in practice from the jurisdiction of the imperial courts and the imperial taxes of the reform of 1495, making them effectively independent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, although formal recognition came only in 1648.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-basel-1499.jpg" alt="Treaty of Basel (1499)" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diebold Schilling the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peace_of_Basel_1499_Negotiations.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
